      "writtenOn": "2017-03-06T17:43:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good point.   If we chose to have only enable/disable then disable would be similar to a delete.  For instance, doing a disable of an olt would bring it to the \"pre-provisioning\" state with all of its onus removed.    I find that too drastic.\n\nWith the activate/disable/re-enable/delete, when disabling an olt then we are just stopping traffic and mark the olt and onus as disabled.  Re-enabling the olt will bring back the olt and onus to their previous states.  I find this approach would give more flexibility to the user.  It\u0027s true that it adds complexity to the code.",
      "parentUuid": "da141535_13262417",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 92,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 100,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "aa131be4a70af6e67031f82206bc24c8c8ec3737",
