      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "da141535_f3697026",
        "filename": "voltha/adapters/interface.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 100,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000004
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-06T17:50:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "OK I see where you were trying to go. Augmenting enable and disable to not clear state unless calls to remove are made would effectively provide the same behaviour no? \n\nImho, enable and disable only mark devices online or offline respectively. Then remove modifies their existence in voltha. Does this make sense?",
      "parentUuid": "da141535_338808e7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 92,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 100,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "aa131be4a70af6e67031f82206bc24c8c8ec3737",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "da141535_b373f814",
        "filename": "voltha/adapters/interface.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 100,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000056
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-06T18:00:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s correct.  The current behavior is as follows:\n\n1) activate_olt -\u003e create the olt and discover the onus\n2) disable -\u003e prevent the device from handling traffic\n3) re-enable -\u003e device is set back to it\u0027s activated state \n4) delete -\u003e remove the device from voltha\n\nMakes sense?",
      "parentUuid": "da141535_f3697026",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 92,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 100,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "aa131be4a70af6e67031f82206bc24c8c8ec3737",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "da141535_73656044",
        "filename": "voltha/adapters/interface.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 100,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000004
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-06T18:03:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "yup i guess my suggestion was to merge activate_olt with re_enable which would mean that enable will activate the olt if it needs to or simple allow the device to forward traffic.",
      "parentUuid": "da141535_b373f814",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 92,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 100,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "aa131be4a70af6e67031f82206bc24c8c8ec3737",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "da141535_335fe874",
        "filename": "voltha/adapters/interface.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 100,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000056
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-06T18:43:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The device state transitions for activate_olt and re-enable are different.  For Activate_olt, the state transitions from pre-provisioned to enabled.  However, for re-enable the state transitions from disabled to enabled.\n\nAre your concerns about the gRPC APIs or the Adapter APIs?  If we want to have a single gRPC API (e.g. enable) then that not an issue.   However, if we want to have a common API for the adapter then that could increase the adapter complexity since the device won\u0027t know the actual state transition that has occurred (unless we hack something in the model to keep the transition, quite ugly).   IMHO, the gRPC API change to a single enable makes sense, but the adapter would still need two APIs (activate and re-enable).   If this is the same code for a given adapter then the adapter can create a single method.\n\nThoughts?",
      "parentUuid": "da141535_73656044",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 92,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 100,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "aa131be4a70af6e67031f82206bc24c8c8ec3737",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
